    "kernel_code": "1: # Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.\n2: \n3: import torch\n4: import triton\n5: import triton.language as tl\n6: \n7: \n8: @triton.jit\n9: def _stable_argsort_kernel(\n10:     keys_ptr,       # [N, W] int64 input (modified in-place: sorted)\n11:     perm_ptr,       # [N, W] int64 output (permutation indices)\n12:     N: tl.constexpr,\n13:     W: tl.constexpr,\n14:     BLOCK_W: tl.constexpr,\n15: ):\n16:     \"\"\"Ascending bitonic sort of each row, returning the permutation.\"\"\"\n17:     pid = tl.program_id(0)\n18:     if pid >= N:\n19:         return\n20: \n21:     offs = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_W)\n22:     mask = offs < W\n23:     base = pid * W\n24: \n25:     keys = tl.load(keys_ptr + base + offs, mask=mask, other=0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)\n26:     perm = offs.to(tl.int64)\n27: \n28:     size = 1\n29:     while size < BLOCK_W:\n30:         stride = size\n31:         while stride > 0:\n32:             partner = offs ^ stride\n33:             ascending = ((offs & (size << 1)) == 0)\n34: \n35:             p_key = tl.load(keys_ptr + base + partner, mask=(partner < W), other=0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)\n36:             p_perm = tl.load(perm_ptr + base + partner, mask=(partner < W), other=0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)\n37: \n38:             is_lower_idx = offs < partner\n39:             want_smaller = (is_lower_idx & ascending) | ((~is_lower_idx) & (~ascending))\n40: \n41:             my_is_smaller = (keys < p_key) | ((keys == p_key) & (perm > p_perm))\n42: \n43:             should_take_partner = (want_smaller & (~my_is_smaller) & (partner < W)) | \\\n44:                                   ((~want_smaller) & my_is_smaller & (partner < W))\n45: \n46:             keys = tl.where(should_take_partner, p_key, keys)\n47:             perm = tl.where(should_take_partner, p_perm, perm)\n48: \n49:             tl.store(keys_ptr + base + offs, keys, mask=mask)\n50:             tl.store(perm_ptr + base + offs, perm, mask=mask)\n51:             tl.debug_barrier()\n52: \n53:             keys = tl.load(keys_ptr + base + offs, mask=mask, other=0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)\n54:             perm = tl.load(perm_ptr + base + offs, mask=mask, other=0)\n55: \n56:             stride = stride >> 1\n57:         size = size << 1\n58: \n59: \n60: def triton_argsort(keys: torch.Tensor):\n61:     \"\"\"Ascending argsort for small rows. Returns (sorted_keys, permutation).\"\"\"\n62:     N, W = keys.shape\n63:     BLOCK_W = triton.next_power_of_2(W)\n64:     keys_out = keys.clone()\n65:     perm = torch.arange(W, device=keys.device, dtype=torch.int64).unsqueeze(0).expand(N, -1).contiguous()\n66:     _stable_argsort_kernel[(N,)](keys_out, perm, N=N, W=W, BLOCK_W=BLOCK_W, num_warps=1)\n67:     return keys_out, perm",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Operation: per-row ascending argsort of small integer keys\n(facebookresearch/sparse-delta-memory, lingua/sparse_delta_memory/triton_argsort.py).\n\n`triton_argsort(keys)` takes an [N, W] int64 tensor and returns the sorted keys\ntogether with the permutation that produces them:\n\n    sorted_keys[n, i] = keys[n, perm[n, i]]\n    sorted_keys[n, :] is non-decreasing\n\nTie rule: the sort must be STABLE. When two entries of a row hold the same key,\nthe one with the LOWER original index must come first. The permutation is used\nto gather memory slots whose contents differ, so which of two tied entries is\nplaced first changes the values that are read out afterwards, and stability is\nwhat makes the read reproducible across runs and across replicas.\n\nInput domain: keys are arbitrary int64 values. Duplicate keys within a row are\nexpected -- the keys are quantized scores, and quantization is what makes two\ndifferent underlying values land on the same key.\n\nDoes triton_argsort() satisfy this contract?\n",
